nvert the string of digits to a list of integers\\n    digits = [int(d) for d in digit_string]\\n    \\n    # Process from right to left\\n    # The rightmost digit is at index len(digits) - 1\\n    # The second from right is at index len(digits) - 2\\n    # We double every second digit from the right (i.e., at odd positions from the right)\\n    for i in range(len(digits) - 1, -1, -1):\\n        n = digits[i]\\n        # Position from right: 0 is rightmost, 1 is second from right, etc.\\n        # If the position from right is odd, it's a 'second' digit.\\n        pos_from_right = (len(digits) - 1 - i)\\n        if pos_from_right % 2 == 1:\\n            n *= 2\\n            # \"add the digits of each product\"\\n            # If n was 10-18, adding digits is same as subtracting 9\\n            if n > 9:\\n                n = (n // 10) + (n % 10)\\n        total += n\\n\\n    return total % 10 == 0"
